[
    {
        "text": "My velocity is increasing quite a lot now, and bugs are much easier to fix. I had a problem that code changes by the inline markdown editor (or by AI) were not picked up by the code editor; its state lagged. I seeded Robocoop context with the `change history`, `inline md editor` and `code editor` notebooks, and asked for a fix, which it one shotted, and now all the editors are in sync by reusing the change-history trick of listening to runtime for code changes.\nArchitecturally this is very pleasing to me, none of the editors know about each other, they are all triggered from runtime-is-the-source of truth, and thus are radically decoupled and I can add additional methods of code authoring (doesn't have to be text based!) without having to do any plumbing to all the others. Multiple views of the same thing!",
